1
00:00:00,320 --> 00:00:01,500
Your airline can make money

2
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:02,760
from you while you're buying

3
00:00:02,760 --> 00:00:03,260
groceries.

4
00:00:03,980 --> 00:00:05,320
No boarding pass required.

5
00:00:06,883 --> 00:00:07,983
The secret is a second

6
00:00:07,983 --> 00:00:09,823
business hiding behind the planes,

7
00:00:10,303 --> 00:00:11,903
selling reward points to banks.

8
00:00:13,403 --> 00:00:14,883
Seats are expensive to sell.

9
00:00:15,823 --> 00:00:17,943
Fuel, crews, aircraft, maintenance,

10
00:00:18,343 --> 00:00:19,863
and airports all need paying

11
00:00:19,863 --> 00:00:21,143
before a flight turns a

12
00:00:21,143 --> 00:00:21,403
profit.

13
00:00:23,017 --> 00:00:24,517
A bank buys miles from

14
00:00:24,517 --> 00:00:26,337
the airline, then awards them

15
00:00:26,337 --> 00:00:27,897
to customers for spending on

16
00:00:27,897 --> 00:00:28,637
its credit card.

17
00:00:30,114 --> 00:00:31,974
Swipe for coffee, pay for

18
00:00:31,974 --> 00:00:33,694
groceries, collect points.

19
00:00:34,334 --> 00:00:35,534
The bank sends cash to

20
00:00:35,534 --> 00:00:37,114
the airline, often before you

21
00:00:37,114 --> 00:00:37,594
take a trip.

22
00:00:39,045 --> 00:00:40,445
Banks want your business, too.

23
00:00:41,245 --> 00:00:42,505
Cards can bring merchant fees,

24
00:00:42,865 --> 00:00:44,205
annual fees, and interest.

25
00:00:44,885 --> 00:00:46,285
Rewards make the card attractive.

26
00:00:47,890 --> 00:00:51,370
In 2025, Delta received $8.2

27
00:00:51,370 --> 00:00:53,350
billion from American Express

28
00:00:53,350 --> 00:00:54,650
through their partnership.

29
00:00:55,410 --> 00:00:56,330
That's a lot of everyday

30
00:00:56,330 --> 00:00:56,770
spending.

31
00:00:58,357 --> 00:00:59,577
But that cash is not

32
00:00:59,577 --> 00:01:00,197
all profit.

33
00:01:00,957 --> 00:01:02,117
Part covers future flights.

34
00:01:02,697 --> 00:01:04,237
Other portions pay for marketing

35
00:01:04,237 --> 00:01:04,897
and benefits.

36
00:01:06,478 --> 00:01:08,418
Filling an otherwise empty seat

37
00:01:08,418 --> 00:01:09,638
may cost less than the

38
00:01:09,638 --> 00:01:10,818
bank paid for the points.

39
00:01:11,438 --> 00:01:12,698
That's the economic appeal.

40
00:01:14,214 --> 00:01:15,434
But rewards aren't free.

41
00:01:16,034 --> 00:01:17,134
A full flight can mean

42
00:01:17,134 --> 00:01:18,794
displacing a paying passenger.

43
00:01:19,734 --> 00:01:21,474
Partner airlines also charge for

44
00:01:21,474 --> 00:01:22,074
award seats.

45
00:01:23,636 --> 00:01:25,316
Some points are never redeemed.

46
00:01:26,356 --> 00:01:27,756
Airlines estimate that breakage.

47
00:01:28,436 --> 00:01:30,196
Changing award prices can also

48
00:01:30,196 --> 00:01:31,696
change what your balance buys.

49
00:01:33,314 --> 00:01:34,634
So, more money from points

50
00:01:34,634 --> 00:01:35,194
than seats?

51
00:01:35,854 --> 00:01:36,934
The headline needs care.

52
00:01:37,914 --> 00:01:39,374
Partnership cash, ticket revenue,

53
00:01:39,554 --> 00:01:40,814
and profit are different measures.

54
00:01:42,373 --> 00:01:43,733
Ticket sales can still be

55
00:01:43,733 --> 00:01:44,433
much larger.

56
00:01:45,113 --> 00:01:46,513
The real story is how

57
00:01:46,513 --> 00:01:48,533
loyalty turns everyday spending

58
00:01:48,533 --> 00:01:50,193
into valuable airline cash.

59
00:01:51,709 --> 00:01:52,989
The plane makes the reward

60
00:01:52,989 --> 00:01:53,669
desirable.

61
00:01:54,309 --> 00:01:55,689
The card keeps cash flowing.

62
00:01:56,249 --> 00:01:57,189
You're part of the airline

63
00:01:57,189 --> 00:01:58,769
business, even on the ground.
